+## HD repair plan — broad issues before page details, 2026-09-29
+
+This section controls the order of HD work. The detailed checklist below is an
+evidence ledger, not permission to spend time polishing one page while a more
+visible or functional problem remains elsewhere. Fix only failures that
+prevent a reliable comparison before starting the Qwen value audit. Continue
+the remaining functional repairs while using its results to guide each asset
+change. Revisit the audit whenever a new asset class enters the game. If a
+later test exposes a higher-severity regression, return to it.
+
+**Working candidate and comparison.** Keep the installed hash-verified
+`Chaos-Wide169-Trial.exe` as the comparison baseline and keep the isolated HD
+candidate and user playtest separate, with separate saves/configuration and
+rollback copies. Capture the baseline first, then the same save, page and
+actions in HD at full 2560×1440 output. Use the threshold-48 difference tool
+to locate changes, inspect the actual controls and interactions, and record
+known baseline defects separately. The Grimoire right feedback tab is one
+documented baseline defect; use the user's correct reference half for it.
+
+| Order | Scope | Work to finish | Exit gate |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1. Comparison blockers | Startup, required page access, capture, saves and render-mode identity | Check hash identity, isolated startup, full-output captures and safe save restoration. Fix only crashes, data-loss risks or page failures that stop representative baseline/HD A/B runs. | Representative UI and battle pages can be captured in both builds with the same verified save/action; mutable files are preserved and UI/battle render modes are confirmed. |
+| 2. Early Qwen value audit | Representative finished assets and one small pilot from each pending class | For menu/illustrated UI, text and controls, realm art, portrait, battle icon, terrain and creature motion, compare the baseline, a plain enlargement at the same target resolution, and the local Qwen result in the game. Capture the same page/action at full output resolution; inspect readability, identity, texture, colour keys, clipping and motion. Record accept/refine/plain-upscale/defer decisions by category. | Each sampled class has an in-game value verdict with paired evidence. The verdict determines whether pending jobs proceed, change canvas/strength/packing, or stop. Edge energy and queue status alone do not pass this gate. |
+| 3. Functional and large visual repairs | Remaining navigation, input, save/load, OGG/FMV and window issues; whole-page geometry, missing or tiny controls, wrong layers, unreadable text and major colour-key errors | Continue the short route across main menu, settings, battle, Esc/save/return, Region Entry, Grimoire, Portmanteau, dialogs and end screens. Exercise primary actions, rank visible failures by impact and fix the largest first. Recheck whether Qwen art improves the actual page; feed poor cases back to phase 2. | Primary routes complete with intact saves/config; every main page has a paired capture and issue disposition; no blocker, missing control, unreadable primary text, wrong scale or major crop remains. |
+| 4. Targeted generation and integration | Remaining local Qwen output, shared resources, animations and material quality | Generate or regenerate by the category verdict and visible page need. Preserve original frame order, offsets, masks and colour keys. Route shared battle/UI assets by page when their target sizes differ. Use a small pilot after every pipeline change before a larger batch. Rerun all assets only if a demonstrated common fault warrants it. | Accepted assets have hash/geometry checks and game A/B evidence against plain enlargement; no accepted replacement breaks battle, saves or another page. Weak categories are deferred or use the better plain enlargement. |
+| 5. Page detail pass | Small icon offsets, glyph strokes, spacing, shadows, colour nuance and low-impact pixel differences | Revisit each page's threshold-48 map and remaining TODO, compare at full output resolution, fix defects with clear visual or interaction benefit, and document intentional HD art differences. | Each page has a final before/after pair, interaction check and a short list of accepted differences or known baseline bugs. |
+| 6. Candidate qualification | Cross-page regressions and runtime compatibility | Repeat the core route, long combat, QoL bindings, save/load, OGG/FMV, window transitions and rollback. Measure 30 logic updates and 60 distinct renders separately without changing gameplay time. Promote a new isolated user playtest only after these gates pass. | Manifest and rollback verified; no required compatibility gate is untested or failing. |
+
+**Qwen feedback loop.** Keep a per-asset decision beside its source hash,
+generated hash, category and in-game capture: `accept`, `refine and rerun`,
+`plain enlargement wins`, or `defer`. A visible improvement means clearer
+important content at its actual rendered size without changed meaning,
+unwanted invented texture, broken lettering, halo/key damage or animation
+flicker. When several samples in one category fail for the same reason,
+adjust that category's Qwen canvas, strength, mask or sheet packing and retest
+a small pilot before resuming its queue. When Qwen adds little value, stop
+spending GPU time on that category. Keep the original, plain enlargement and
+Qwen variant available for reversible comparison; never substitute another
+generator for the user's local Qwen Image 2.1.
+
+**Next actions in order.** First confirm that representative baseline/HD
+captures and save restoration remain reliable. Start the Qwen game A/B pilot
+immediately using existing reachable pages and finished assets; do not wait
+for every page interaction to be fixed. Feed its verdict into the pending 160
+SPR containers and into any regenerated UI art. Continue Portmanteau
+drag/drop, equipment and QoL repairs and the remaining route/visual issues
+with this evidence in hand. The remaining tiny Portmanteau talisman mark, individual glyph
+strokes and similar per-page details wait for phase 5. Missing latest
+test2/test7 fixtures are tracked below;
+use explicitly hash-verified legacy fixtures for routes they can cover and
+record which checks require the newer saves.
