-## Two rules that were expensive to learn
-
-**All outputs are PNG.** JPEG is banned. A colour-key field must stay exact or the engine
-stops keying it out, and a second lossy encode moves key pixels by up to 8 levels at
-quality 95. PNG is lossless. This changes the extension of JPEG and BMP sources, so the
-engine side has to accept PNG at those paths.
-
-**Colour-key masks are restored byte for byte.** Old assets make transparency with a key
-colour, not an alpha channel: pure magenta or blue in palette art, 251,0,253 and 0,0,254
-in JPEG sources. The keyed region plus a two pixel rim is copied back from a
-nearest-neighbour resample of the original after the model runs. Detection found 28 of 60
-sampled assets keyed, covering 9% to 99% of the image. Verified byte for byte over 3.4
-million pixels: maximum difference 0. Without it the model mottles the flat key field and
-Lanczos leaves a halo at the sprite edge.
-
-## Canvas tier is per record, not global
-
-`preset_tier` is decided at plan time: the **2048** class for UI art, the **1024** class
-for animation frames, terrain and other small art. Native 800x600 UI measured **+288%**
-edge energy at 2048 against **+87%** at 1024; a 2048-class job costs about 50 s against
-8.7 s. Where a small UI asset already reaches its target scale on the cheaper preset the
-planner keeps that preset. **Do not reintroduce a global tier.**
-
-## Taking over
-
-```powershell
-python modernization/tools/hd_pipeline.py plan     # rebuild queue, skeleton and list
-python modernization/tools/hd_pipeline.py status   # what is done and pending
-python modernization/tools/hd_pipeline.py run --route composite --category ui-800x600 --category ui-untiered
-```
-
-`run` skips records already done and retries anything failed, so any command is safe to
-repeat and a killed batch resumes where it stopped. The queue is written every ten
-assets. A trial limited with `--max-sheets` is recorded as `partial`, not `done`, so
-the rest of the container is not silently skipped.
-
-Re-planning preserves the status of every record whose source hash, target size, preset,
-strength and route are unchanged, so changing a setting resets exactly what it affects.
-
-## What is deliberately not built
-
-| Group | Files | Why |
-| --- | ---: | --- |
-| Legacy 640x480 tier | 424 | Same artwork at the legacy resolution; including it would give one portrait two output sizes. |
-| Cursors (`.cur`) | 20 | The preset floor forces about 24x, so the model invents rather than restores. Deferred by the user. |
-| `.ani` sequence definitions | 136 | Not image data: a sprite name plus a table of frame indices. Frame count and order are preserved, so they stay valid unchanged. |
-| Legacy SPR version 2 | 7 | Frame table layout still undecoded; small early UI sprites, low value. |
-
-## Invariants for any further work
-
-- **Nothing may be installed into the game.** No generated image has been loaded by the
-  engine and no native 1920x1440 UI mode is proven.
-- **Geometry is never generated.** Every output is a Lanczos resample of the original plus
-  a gated high-frequency band. If a change makes the model supply structure, it is wrong.
-- **Alpha and colour keys are never generated.** Both are taken from the original.
-- **Never treat an atlas as an animation, or the reverse.** Route changes the measured
-  gain by about a factor of two.
-- **Canvas tier is per record.**
-- Every asset has a JSON manifest with source and output SHA-256 and the Manager job id.
-  Do not hand-edit outputs.
-
